35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, transport is a huge part of the cost if we go far! Also, whole-building lets are risky because if someone drops out late, the rest of us have to pay for them.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I've learned that the seniors believe the only way the different year-groups truly bond is during the evenings when everyone sleeps in the same place. Also, some members never attend away camps.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The canteen closes during vacation, meaning we'd have to cook for ourselves, which took the duty pair two hours a day last year. Also, public bookings require a tedious lottery and a nine-page application.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The public beds are cheap, but the clubs that went inland said they had to sleep eight people to a room and had a strict eleven o'clock lights-out! That sounds way too strict!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The club hall is already quite crowded with other clubs, so we'd be split between early mornings and late nights. Plus, a third of our members can't even make it by nine without a bed.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, if a third of the members need a bed anyway, does that make staying on campus more expensive than we thought? It seems like we'd be paying for separate rooms regardless.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"That is a very good question, Mio. If we want the year-groups to bond, having some members in separate rooms while others commute might hinder that closeness.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, it does. Between the fragmented hall schedule and the need for separate accommodation, the ""local"" option is less convenient and potentially more costly than it appears.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"If the inland places are too strict and the campus is a mess, maybe the seaside lodge is better? But @Mio, you said those whole-building things are risky if people cancel!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"Exactly. The financial risk of a whole-building let is high, but the logistical nightmare of the campus hall is also a serious concern. We need to weigh the cost against the actual usability.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"If we go with the lodge, we have to be really careful about the headcount. But @Shizue, if we want everyone to bond, isn't a private lodge better than eight people in one room?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"It certainly would be more comfortable, and a private environment often encourages more natural conversations than a crowded dormitory. However, we must consider if the cost might discourage some from attending.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Rin, the inland option isn't just about the rules; the administrative burden of that nine-page application and the lottery is a significant risk if our dates shift. It's not a reliable choice.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I didn't think about the paperwork! If the lottery is that scary and the rooms are cramped, then the Mountain Training Centre is totally out. What about the lodge?","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"The lodge seems like the most viable option for bonding and logistics, but the non-refundable deposit is a major red flag for the budget. We can't afford another deficit.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I agree with Misaki. We can't risk a deficit, but we also can't have a camp where people can't even get to the hall on time or sleep properly. Maybe we can find a way to secure the headcount?","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"Perhaps we could ask for a small, non-refundable commitment fee from each member? That way, we ensure the headcount is stable and the financial burden doesn't fall on a few.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,That is a practical solution to mitigate the risk of the whole-building let. It would protect the club's budget while avoiding the administrative nightmare of the public lottery and the cooking duties of the campus.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I'm for the lodge! It sounds way more fun than a strict dormitory or a crowded hall, and if we can fix the money part, it's the best choice!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I'm still cautious about the budget, but compared to the other options, the lodge is the only one that doesn't create a logistical or administrative disaster. If we can guarantee the funds, I'll agree.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
